WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
The last line is typed.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.810
The student sits back.

3
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:04.810
Done.

4
00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.280
Then a second document opens.

5
00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:10.130
It's blank, and it's called Commentary.

6
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.350
On the scales, that blank page
weighs a surprising amount.

7
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.220
The story's already written.

8
00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:19.750
So why would explaining
it be worth so many marks?

9
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.980
In this mission, you'll
learn to study a style model:

10
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:26.140
a published text in your
genre that you learn from.

11
00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:29.200
You'll ask whether a commentary
just retells the story,

12
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:30.740
or does something more.

13
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:34.600
And you'll try it out on the
opening of an invented travel blog.

14
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:39.020
Your mission: explain why the
commentary is worth so many marks.
